---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { href } from "../lib/paths";
import { loadEdgar } from "../lib/edgar";
import { loadProvenance } from "../lib/statutes";

const provenance = loadProvenance();
const edgar = loadEdgar();
const description = "Where the statute index and the EDGAR snapshot come from, and what this site does not copy.";
---

<Base title="Sources and currency" description={description} crumbs={[{ label: "Sources" }]}>
  <p class="kicker">Provenance</p>
  <h1>Sources and currency</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    Section numbers are read out of the House Office of the Law Revision Counsel’s USLM XML.
    Nothing on this site is scraped from a commercial treatise.
  </p>

  <h2>United States Code</h2>
  <p>
    Title 15, chapters 2A and 2B, release <strong>{provenance.release.docPublicationName}</strong>,
    {provenance.release.currencyNote.toLowerCase()}. The XML was created {provenance.release.created}.
    The OLRC marks Title 15 <code>is-positive-law: {provenance.release.positiveLaw}</code>, so the Acts, not the Code, are the positive law.
  </p>
  <p>
    File: <a href={provenance.source}>{provenance.source}</a><br />
    SHA-256: <span class="cite">{provenance.zipSha256}</span><br />
    Index built {provenance.generatedAt}.
  </p>
  <p>{provenance.method}</p>
  <p>
    Each section links to the
    <a href="https://uscode.house.gov/">House OLRC</a> prelim text,
    the <a href="https://www.govinfo.gov/link/uscode/15/77e">govinfo link service</a>,
    and <a href="https://www.law.cornell.edu/uscode/text/15">Cornell’s Legal Information Institute</a>.
    The section pages quote the operative text from that XML, which is United States government work.
    Source credits and amendment notes sit under the text. The same official links stay on every section.
  </p>
  <p>
    The Trust Indenture Act is Title III of the same chapter. It is indexed under its own section numbers
    so a Trust Indenture Act § 304 is never presented as a Securities Act § 304.
    Provisions codified in chapter 2B without an Exchange Act section number (several Dodd-Frank reports,
    parts of the FCPA, transition sections) are listed separately.
  </p>

  <h2>EDGAR</h2>
  <p>
    Tickers come from <a href={edgar.tickerSource}>{edgar.tickerSource}</a> and the SEC exchange file.
    Filings come from <a href="https://data.sec.gov/submissions/">data.sec.gov/submissions</a>.
    Snapshot {edgar.generatedAt}. {edgar.companyCount.toLocaleString("en-US")} issuers,
    {edgar.withFilings.toLocaleString("en-US")} with filings stored.
  </p>
  <p>{edgar.note}</p>
  <p>
    The bulk job sends <span class="cite">{edgar.userAgent}</span> and stays under the SEC’s
    10-requests-per-second fair-access ceiling. A browser cannot set that User-Agent, and
    <code>data.sec.gov</code> has not been a stable CORS source, so the filing list is prebuilt
    and served from this site. Every company page still deep-links to the live EDGAR browse page,
    the classic company index, and EDGAR full-text search with the form and date filter filled in.
    Use those when the snapshot is not enough, especially for a high-volume filer whose older
    periodic reports have fallen out of the SEC “recent” list.
  </p>

  <h2>What is not here yet</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Regulation S-K, Regulation S-X, and the 1933 and 1934 Act rules (17 C.F.R. Parts 229, 210, 230, 239, 240, 249).</li>
    <li>SEC forms, cross-linked back to the sections they implement.</li>
    <li>Adopting, proposing, and interpretive releases, with Federal Register pinpoints.</li>
    <li>Corporation Finance C&amp;DIs, and the amending acts as their own pages.</li>
    <li>SIPA, the Investment Company Act, the Advisers Act, and the freestanding Sarbanes-Oxley provisions in chapter 98.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    The section records already have empty <span class="cite">crossLinks</span> arrays
    (<span class="cite">rules</span>, <span class="cite">forms</span>, <span class="cite">releases</span>,
    <span class="cite">interpretations</span>, <span class="cite">amendingActs</span>) so those layers can be attached
    without changing the section URLs. Paths reserved for them are in the README:
    <span class="cite">/rules/</span>, <span class="cite">/forms/</span>, <span class="cite">/releases/</span>,
    <span class="cite">/cdi/</span>, <span class="cite">/history/</span>.
  </p>
  <p><a href={href()}>Back to Pinpoint</a></p>
</Base>
